<title>UK: TABLE - BA profits rise in year.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BA profits rise in year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			    (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		55.7		   vs 49.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 10.80		  vs 9.80</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 15.05		  vs 13.65</p>
<p> Pretax		     640		    vs 585</p>
<p> Turnover		   8.34 bln	     vs 7.76 bln</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 600 and 630 million stg.</p>
<p>BA results included an exceptional charge of 127 million stg to cover restructuring costs.  </p>
<p>Profit was boosted by an exceptional gain of 125 million stg as a result of restating at original cost its investment in USAirways, reversing the 50 percent write-down made two years ago.  </p>
<p>    Overall load factor   70.3 pct	  vs 70.7</p>
<p>    Passenger load factor 73.2 pct	  vs 73.8</p>
<p>    Passenger (million)   33.44	     vs 32.27</p>
<p>    Cargo (tonnes)	  721		 vs 672</p>
<p>Passenger revenue</p>
<p>    per RPK		   6.47p	     vs 6.39</p>
<p>Cargo revenue</p>
<p>    per CTK		   14.78p	    vs 16.04p</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
